UI/UX Studio
=======

UI/UX Studio combines, rewrites and extends material from the following projects. Where text or
rules were adapted, the original licence terms apply to that material.

- frontend-design (anthropics/skills), Apache License 2.0.
  Adapted: the design-studio stance, grounding in the subject, the AI-look clusters, the
  two-pass plan-and-review process, restraint and self-critique, and writing guidance.
  Modified and reorganised (references 13, 14, 15, 12).

- ui-ux-pro-max (nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill), MIT License.
  Adapted: the priority order, the rule quick-reference, design dials, the Master and page
  override pattern, the pre-delivery checklist and pro rules, and motion and stack guidance
  distilled from its data files (references 04, 10, 11, 17, 19, 20). The style, palette and
  font databases were not included.

- web-design-guidelines (vercel-labs/agent-skills), rules from vercel-labs/web-interface-guidelines
  at commit 434b7f91364665f2f733b310ec54809bf8f37937.
  Included with light edits as reference 18, with the audit output format.

- humanizer-zh (op7418/humanizer-zh), MIT License, itself based on blader/humanizer and
  hardikpandya/stop-slop.
  Adapted: the editing constraints and pattern categories, rewritten for UI copy in any
  language (reference 13, part B).

- product-ui-ux and sutro-design (the author's own skills).
  Basis of the method, templates, contrast script and the project overlay pattern.
